WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.204
-Our next guest is the host of
"The Ali Kolbert Show,"

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:05.638
available at Apple Podcasts.

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:08.408
Please welcome the very funny
Ali Kolbert!

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:10.443
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:16.048 --> 00:00:18.885
-Hi, you guys! Oh, my God.

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:21.721
It is so good to be back on
"The Tonight Show"!

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.956
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.956 --> 00:00:26.693
I just got my booster,

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:30.430
so I can finally see
my family this Thanksgiving!

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.897
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:31.897 --> 00:00:38.003
Oh, not the shot, the seat.
I'm leaving the kids table.

00:00:38.003 --> 00:00:41.373
I finally get to be at eyeline.

00:00:41.373 --> 00:00:46.279
I am fun-sized, so I get hit on
by a lot of young dudes.

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:50.182
Like 10-year-old boys
coming up to me being like,

00:00:50.182 --> 00:00:53.586
"What's your
favorite color, mama?"

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:56.956
I was at the grocery store
the other day with my friend.

00:00:56.956 --> 00:01:01.761
And my friend is my age, but she
looks like an adult human woman.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.829
And this little boy goes up
to her and he says,

00:01:03.829 --> 00:01:05.264
"Excuse me, miss.

00:01:05.264 --> 00:01:08.835
I really like your daughter."

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:10.703
I was like,
"Dude, how old are you?

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:13.772
Do you even have an allowance?"

00:01:13.772 --> 00:01:16.309
He was like,
"Yeah, I have an allowance."

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:19.579
So, going to his Little League
game tomorrow.

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:21.581
Go, Rangers!

00:01:23.048 --> 00:01:24.350
I figured this out --

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.318
that there's two types of men
in the world, okay?

00:01:26.318 --> 00:01:28.755
There's a nice guy
and a shady guy.

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:32.091
And your nice guy
is Amazon, okay?

00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:36.028
Your shady guy is USPS.

00:01:36.028 --> 00:01:38.530
Amazon's always hitting you up
with updates --

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:40.266
"I'll be right there."

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:43.536
USPS, you're like,
"Hey, where are you?"

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:47.073
And he's just like,
"Somewhere in New Jersey, baby."

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:50.976
I'm like, "I thought you were
coming over."

00:01:50.976 --> 00:01:52.745
He's like, "Stay home between
12:00 and 6:00.

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.547
Maybe I'll swing by."

00:01:56.215 --> 00:02:00.119
Amazon's super-excited.
He comes immediately.

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:03.456
He's like,
"How was that for you?"

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:07.961
USPS is like, "Yo, can I leave
my package unprotected?"

00:02:12.798 --> 00:02:15.835
I think dudes
talk a big game, you know?

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:18.037
They're like,
"Let me take you out."

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:22.575
I'm like, "You don't know what
a top sheet is, Connor.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.343
We're not going out.

00:02:24.343 --> 00:02:26.746
You own one towel."

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:30.283
I've met guys who swear they
have two towels.

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:34.520
They have one towel
that's ripped in half.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.723
That is not two.

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:42.161
I feel like the sexism in
this country's out of control.

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:46.966
Like, a dude hooks up with a ton
of women, "Oh, he's a player."

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:51.104
I hook up with a ton of women,
"Oh, lesbian!"

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:55.141
Not cool.

00:02:56.742 --> 00:02:59.612
I did get a girlfriend
over the pandemic.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:03.282
And these girlfriends --
they ask a lot of questions.

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:04.716
My girlfriend's
got a lot of questions.

00:03:04.716 --> 00:03:05.818
She wants to have a baby.

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.853
She's like,
"Who's going to carry?

00:03:07.853 --> 00:03:10.456
Who's doing IVF?
Whose sperm are we using?"

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:11.758
I'm like, "I got a question.

00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:14.860
Who's doing this with you, okay?

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:17.396
'Cause I'm out. No deal."

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.498
That's how I talk now
that I've seen

00:03:19.498 --> 00:03:22.601
every single episode of
"Shark Tank."

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:24.269
I'm like, "I'll never
make my money back

00:03:24.269 --> 00:03:25.437
on a toddler, sweetheart.

00:03:25.437 --> 00:03:27.240
I'm out.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.275
No deal."

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:35.881
I think it's interesting how
you figure out your sexuality.

00:03:35.881 --> 00:03:39.085
Like, when I was younger,
we would play spin the bottle.

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:42.020
And if a girl spun the bottle
and it landed on

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:46.391
another girl, everyone would be
like, "Oh, redo."

00:03:46.391 --> 00:03:50.129
And I'd always be like,
"Stick to the rules, okay?!

00:03:52.965 --> 00:03:55.501
I respect the integrity
of this game!

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.470
Pucker up, Jenna!"

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:03.809
And, like, I was in
a sorority in college.

00:04:03.809 --> 00:04:05.511
That's quite the conundrum --

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:08.514
to be a lesbian in a sorority,

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:11.884
'cause everyone's just like,
"We are sisters!"

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:15.387
And I'm like, "Not by blood!"

00:04:15.387 --> 00:04:19.691
"We can still do stuff.
I didn't join this for family!"

00:04:19.691 --> 00:04:22.562
Thank you so much.
I'm Ali Kolbert!

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:24.563
♪♪
Thank you, guys.

00:04:24.563 --> 00:04:27.667
-Ah! I love...
[ Laughs ]

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:28.767
Oh, my God.

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:32.605
Oh, Ali Kolbert!
Ali Kolbert!

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:35.908
"The Ali Kolbert show"
is available at Apple Podcasts.

